From: SystemG
Subject: Find a session by its scope name when looking up a PID

Debian's libsystemd0-compatible cgroups layout puts sessions in
user.slice/user-UID.slice/session-ID.scope, but nothing fills session_units,
so GetSessionByPID fails for every process except a session leader.
---
--- a/src/login/logind-core.c
+++ b/src/login/logind-core.c
@@ -396,6 +396,17 @@
                 r = cg_pidref_get_unit(pid, &unit);
                 if (r >= 0)
                         s = hashmap_get(m->session_units, unit);
+                /* session_start_cgroup() creates session-ID.scope but never
+                 * registers it in session_units, so the lookup above only ever
+                 * finds nothing: look the session up by the ID in its scope
+                 * name instead. Without this, only a session's leader belongs
+                 * to it (rootless Xorg, gnome-shell, ... get NoSessionForPID). */
+                if (!s) {
+                        _cleanup_free_ char *id = NULL;
+
+                        if (cg_pid_get_session(pid->pid, &id) >= 0)
+                                s = hashmap_get(m->sessions, id);
+                }
 #else // 0
                 log_debug_elogind("Searching session for PID %d", pid->pid);
                 r = cg_pid_get_session(pid->pid, &session_name);
